@szarnyasg I think the problem is located in the `duckdb_extract_statements` function of the C-API. I was able to reproduce the SIGABRT with the following C program:

```
#include "duckdb.h"

duckdb_database db;
duckdb_connection con;

int main() {
	if (duckdb_open(NULL, &db) == DuckDBError) {
		// handle error
	}
	if (duckdb_connect(db, &con) == DuckDBError) {
		// handle error
	}

	duckdb_extracted_statements stmts;
	idx_t foo = duckdb_extract_statements(con, "PRAGMA something", &stmts);

	// cleanup
	duckdb_disconnect(&con);
	duckdb_close(&db);
}
```

Replacing `PRAGMA something` with `PRAGMA show_tables` works, as this command exists.
